      "quiz_k2_1_fb1": "While some water soaks into the ground, puddles on sidewalks and streets mostly disappear because the sun heats them up into vapor.",
      "quiz_k2_1_fb3": "Wind can help water evaporate faster by moving air, but the sun's heat is the main reason liquid water changes into gas.",
      "quiz_k2_1_fb4": "Water molecules never sleep! The sun's energy makes them move faster and float up into the sky.",
      "quiz_k2_1_opt1": "The ground drinks it",
      "quiz_k2_1_opt2": "The sun heats the water",
      "quiz_k2_1_opt3": "Wind blows it away",
      "quiz_k2_1_opt4": "It goes to sleep",
      "quiz_k2_1_q": "What makes puddles disappear on sunny days?",
      "quiz_k2_2_fb1": "Clouds look soft like cotton, but they are actually made of billions of tiny liquid water droplets floating in the air.",
      "quiz_k2_2_fb3": "Smoke comes from fires, but clouds in the sky are made of clean water droplets and ice crystals.",
      "quiz_k2_2_fb4": "Air bubbles are trapped inside water, but clouds are water droplets trapped in the air!",
      "quiz_k2_2_opt1": "Cotton",
      "quiz_k2_2_opt2": "Tiny water drops",
      "quiz_k2_2_opt3": "Smoke",
      "quiz_k2_2_opt4": "Air bubbles",
      "quiz_k2_2_q": "What are clouds made of?",
      "quiz_k2_3_fb1": "Stars are huge, burning suns far away in space. They do not fall from clouds!",
      "quiz_k2_3_fb3": "Leaves fall from trees in autumn, not from clouds in the sky.",
      "quiz_k2_3_fb4": "Rocks are heavy parts of the ground. Only liquid or frozen water falls from clouds.",
      "quiz_k2_3_opt1": "Stars",
      "quiz_k2_3_opt2": "Rain and snow",
      "quiz_k2_3_opt3": "Leaves",
      "quiz_k2_3_opt4": "Rocks",
      "quiz_k2_3_q": "What falls from clouds?",
      "quiz_k2_4_fb1": "Water does not vanish! It collects in lakes, flows down rivers, and fills the oceans.",
      "quiz_k2_4_fb2": "Rain must collect on the ground first before the sun can heat it to rise back up later.",
      "quiz_k2_4_fb4": "Earth's gravity keeps water on our planet. It collects in oceans and lakes rather than escaping into space.",
      "quiz_k2_4_opt1": "It disappears",
      "quiz_k2_4_opt2": "Back up to the sky",
      "quiz_k2_4_opt3": "Rivers, lakes, and oceans",
      "quiz_k2_4_opt4": "Into outer space",
      "quiz_k2_4_q": "Where does rain go after it falls?",
      "quiz_k2_5_fb1": "Leaves can absorb a tiny bit of moisture, but plants get almost all their water by drinking it from the soil through their roots.",
      "quiz_k2_5_fb3": "Flowers attract bees and make seeds, but they do not drink water from the soil.",
      "quiz_k2_5_fb4": "All living things need water to survive, including plants!",
      "quiz_k2_5_opt1": "Through their leaves",
      "quiz_k2_5_opt2": "Through their roots",
      "quiz_k2_5_opt3": "Through their flowers",
      "quiz_k2_5_opt4": "They don't drink water",
      "quiz_k2_5_q": "How do plants drink water?",
      "quiz_k2_6_fb1": "The sun provides warm heat, which warms water up instead of freezing it into ice.",
      "quiz_k2_6_fb3": "Algae and plants can make water look green, but the sun heats it up so it evaporates.",
      "quiz_k2_6_fb4": "Ocean water is already salty because of dissolved minerals, not because of the sun.",
      "quiz_k2_6_opt1": "Freezes it",
      "quiz_k2_6_opt2": "Heats it up so it rises as vapor",
      "quiz_k2_6_opt3": "Turns it green",
      "quiz_k2_6_opt4": "Makes it salty",
      "quiz_k2_6_q": "What does the sun do to ocean water?",
      "quiz_k2_7_fb2": "Stars are massive bodies in space, whereas water vapor just condenses into cloud droplets.",
      "quiz_k2_7_fb3": "Water vapor gas is invisible, but when it cools and condenses, it becomes visible liquid droplets (clouds).",
      "quiz_k2_7_fb4": "Water does not catch fire! Cooling vapor turns back into liquid water.",
      "quiz_k2_7_opt1": "It turns into cloud drops",
      "quiz_k2_7_opt2": "It becomes a star",
      "quiz_k2_7_opt3": "It stays invisible",
      "quiz_k2_7_opt4": "It catches fire",
      "quiz_k2_7_q": "What happens when water vapor gets cold up high?",
      "quiz_k2_8_fb1": "Groundwater is part of the cycle. It flows slowly and emerges at natural springs or is pumped up through wells.",
      "quiz_k2_8_fb3": "Digger wells do reach groundwater, but natural springs bubble up to the surface without any digging.",
      "quiz_k2_8_fb4": "Springs flow continuously, even on sunny days, because groundwater moves very slowly.",
      "quiz_k2_8_opt1": "No, never",
      "quiz_k2_8_opt2": "Yes, through springs and wells",
      "quiz_k2_8_opt3": "Only if you dig",
      "quiz_k2_8_opt4": "Only on rainy days",
      "quiz_k2_8_q": "Can water underground come back up?",
