      "male_approaches_female_some_species_us": "Male approaches female. Some species use elaborate visual displays (Caribbean reef octopus stripes); others mate hidden from females (sneaker tactic). Male inserts a sperm packet (spermatophore) into the female mantle cavity via the hectocotylus arm. Female stores sperm; she can fertilize eggs days or weeks later.",
      "male_octopuses_have_a_specialized_arm_": "Male octopuses have a specialized arm called the hectocotylus — modified for sperm transfer. In Argonaut argonauts, the hectocotylus detaches and swims to the female on its own. Early naturalists thought it was a parasitic worm.",
