      "touch_ceiling_wall_perch_rest": "Touch ceiling/wall: Perch & rest",
      "track_prey_route": "Track prey route",
      "trees_give_strong_woody_echoes_water_p": "Trees give strong woody echoes. Water pools reflect dimly. Moths flit erratically — they're hard to track!",
      "trees_may_communicate_through_sound_st": "Trees may communicate through sound: studies show plant roots produce clicking sounds at 220 Hz, and neighboring roots grow toward these sounds. \"Talking trees\" may be more than a metaphor.",
      "tropical_rainforest": "Tropical Rainforest",
      "tropical_rainforests_are_loud_in_the_u": "Tropical rainforests are loud in the ultrasonic. White-nose syndrome has killed 6+ million North American bats since 2006; insect populations downstream are visibly affected. A frequency band we never knew about.",
      "try_another_doppler_challenge": "Try another Doppler challenge",
      "try_it": "Try it: ",
      "turn_off_unnecessary_outdoor_lights_li": "Turn off unnecessary outdoor lights. Light pollution disrupts bat foraging and insect availability.",
      "ultrasonic_canes_and_wearable_devices_": "Ultrasonic canes and wearable devices help blind individuals navigate by converting sonar echoes into vibrations or audio tones — giving humans a form of echolocation.",
      "ultrasound_imaging_sends_1_20_mhz_puls": "Ultrasound imaging sends 1-20 MHz pulses into the body and builds images from echoes. The same physics as echolocation, just at higher frequencies and through tissue instead of air.",
      "untreated_plywood_or_cedar_never_press": "Untreated plywood or cedar (never pressure-treated — toxic to bats), wood screws, exterior caulk, dark exterior paint or stain",
