      "no_evolution_disproves_the_origin_of_l": "No — evolution disproves the origin of life",
      "no_evolution_explains_how_life_diversi": "No — evolution explains how life DIVERSIFIES once it exists; the origin of life itself is a separate field called abiogenesis",
      "no_evolution_is_directionless_it_just_": "No — evolution is directionless; it just optimizes for survival in current conditions",
      "no_evolution_is_fully_directed_by_an_e": "No — evolution is fully directed by an external force",
      "no_fitness_pressure_watch_how_the_popu": "No fitness pressure. Watch how the population still changes over generations from random sampling (genetic drift). Smaller populations drift harder.",
      "no_forces": "No forces: ",
      "no_giraffes_were_created_with_long_nec": "No — giraffes were created with long necks",
      "no_humans_and_modern_monkeys_share_a_c": "No, humans and modern monkeys share a common ancestor that lived ~25-30 million years ago",
      "no_humans_evolved_separately_from_any_": "No, humans evolved separately from any other primate",
      "no_most_mutations_are_neutral_some_are": "No — most mutations are neutral; some are harmful; some are beneficial",
      "no_mutations_are_random_but_selection_": "No — mutations are random, but selection is non-random (it favors traits that boost survival/reproduction)",
      "no_only_changes_to_dna_can_be_inherite": "No — only changes to DNA can be inherited; muscles built in life don't change DNA",
      "no_selection_happens_because_individua": "No — selection happens because individuals with longer necks happened to leave more offspring; no \"need\" causes mutations to appear",
      "non_random_mating": "Non-random mating",
      "not_all_evolution_is_selection_random_": "not all evolution is selection. Random change is real, especially in small populations. Conservation biologists worry about this for endangered species — even with perfect protection, a tiny population loses genetic diversity by drift alone.",
      "not_modeled_here_and_small_population_": " (not modeled here) and small population size (genetic drift) are the other two.",
      "note_your_time_to_eat_10_in_round_1_co": "Note your time to eat 10 in Round 1. Compare to your time in Round 10. You'll be SLOWER even though you're more practiced — because the prey are evolving to evade YOU.",
      "now_here_you_see_it_takes_all_the_runn": "\"Now, here, you see, it takes all the running you can do, to keep in the same place.\" — Lewis Carroll, Through the Looking-Glass. Predators select prey to be faster; prey selects predators to be faster. Both populations escalate together — neither getting ahead. Real examples: cheetahs vs gazelles, bats vs moths, plants vs caterpillars.",
      "offspring_variation_model_limit": "Larger offspring variation can speed movement toward an optimum while also maintaining broader trait distributions. This slider is not a biological mutation-rate estimate.",
      "often_emerges_after_antibiotic_treatme": "Often emerges AFTER antibiotic treatment for something else. The antibiotic kills off normal gut bacteria, leaving room for resistant C. diff to take over. ~12,800 US deaths/year.",
      "on_the_directional_preset_with_selecti": "On the directional preset with selection ON, set Mutation Size to 0 (no variation introduced). After convergence the population stops changing — selection has nothing left to act on. Then bump Mutation Size up — convergence resumes faster.",
      "once_large_beaked_birds_dominate_turni": "Once large-beaked birds dominate, turning off drought is not enough — the small-beak gene pool may already be too thin to recover quickly. This is why evolution often doesn't fully reverse even when conditions revert.",
      "one_full_period_per_major_module": "· One full period per major module",
      "one_way_mutation_model": ": this simplified control models A → a only. Reverse mutation is not included.",
      "one_way_mutation_rate_model_limit": "One-way A → a mutation probability per modeled generation. Real rates vary by organism and locus and are generally far below this deliberately exaggerated teaching range.",
      "only_intelligent_species_have_evolutio": "Only intelligent species have evolutionary direction",
      "only_some_humans_evolved_from_monkeys": "Only some humans evolved from monkeys",
      "open_curriculum_guide": "→ Open Curriculum Guide",
      "open_each_module_before_class_to_verif": "Open each module before class to verify it loads correctly and to see what controls students will see. Each module has its own collapsible 🍎 Teacher Notes section with NGSS standards, common misconceptions, and extension activities.",
