      "most_migrants_fly_between_5_000_15_000": "Most migrants fly between 5,000-15,000 feet. Air temperature drops ~3.5°F per 1,000 feet (standard lapse rate). Birds choose altitude to find favorable winds — the same bird may fly at 2,000 feet one night and 12,000 the next.",
