      "aldus_manutius_3": "Aldus Manutius",
      "aldus_manutius_of_venice_1452_1515_is_": "Aldus Manutius of Venice (1452-1515) is credited with popularizing the octavo edition for serious literature. Before Aldus, classical Latin + Greek texts were always printed in folio or quarto — large, expensive, library-bound. Starting around 1501, Aldus printed classical texts in compact octavo editions priced for individual scholars + traveling clerics. The Aldine octavo is the direct ancestor of the modern paperback. Cost: roughly 1/8 of an equivalent folio. Result: an explosion in personal libraries among the educated middle class.",
      "alexandria_monastery_libraries_univers": "Alexandria → monastery libraries → universities → Carnegie public libraries → digital archives. The institutional partner of print.",
