      "maine_had_multiple_rag_based_paper_mil": "Maine had multiple rag-based paper mills in the 1800s — Yarmouth Paper Mill, Eldridge Mill (Pittsfield), and several along the Kennebec. Maine's shift from rag to wood-pulp papermaking in the late 1800s — driven by the abundance of spruce + the technology of Hugh Burgess and J. C. Mengel — is one chapter in why central Maine became a paper-mill economy that lasted into the 21st century. Modern Sappi (Westbrook + Skowhegan) descended from these wood-pulp pioneers.",
