      "try_again_4": "↺ Try again",
      "try_it_read_the_type": "🪞 Try it: read the type",
      "try_next": "Try next: ",
      "try_this_one_again": "Try this one again",
      "try_your_name_the_date_or_any_short_ph": "Try your name, the date, or any short phrase.",
      "tsien_tsuen_hsuin_paper_and_printing_i": "Tsien Tsuen-Hsuin, \"Paper and Printing\" in Joseph Needham, Science and Civilisation in China vol. 5 part 1 (1985)",
      "tsien_tsuen_hsuin_paper_and_printing_i_2": "Tsien Tsuen-Hsuin, \"Paper and Printing\" in Joseph Needham, Science and Civilisation in China vol. 5 part 1 (1985)",
      "tunes_the_drying_rate_and_consistency_": "Tunes the drying rate and consistency for the season. Hot summer ink is mixed differently from cold winter ink. This is artisan judgment, not a fixed formula.",
      "tv_radio_guides": "TV/radio guides",
      "tyndale_luther_the_king_james_committe": "Tyndale + Luther + the King James committee + modern Bible translation + literary translation today. How language crosses through print.",
      "tyndale_s_english_new_testament_1526": "Tyndale's English New Testament (1526)",
      "type_alloy_is_mostly_lead_compositors_": "Type alloy is mostly lead. Compositors picked up sorts thousands of times a day; casters worked over molten metal. Chronic low-dose lead exposure produced the \"printer's palsy\" that 19th-century occupational physicians documented. Modern letterpress shops use polymer plates or photopolymer instead.",
      "type_any_printing_press_question_the_a": "Type any printing-press question. The AI grounds its answer in the same sources cited throughout this lab. ",
      "type_cooper_at_the_cooper_union_type_d": "Type@Cooper at the Cooper Union — type-design education",
      "type_cooper_typography_history_and_edu": "Type@Cooper — Typography history and education",
      "type_designer": "Type designer",
      "type_forme": "Type forme",
      "type_forme_mirrored": "Type forme (mirrored)",
      "type_foundry_workshop": "Type Foundry Workshop",
      "type_history": "Type history",
      "type_size_pt": "Type size (pt)",
      "type_the_readable_word": "Type the readable word…",
      "type_your_name": "Type your name…",
      "type_your_name_a_word_or_a_short_phras": "Type your name, a word, or a short phrase. See it set in five typefaces from across the printed centuries. Each one was the default of its era. Your name in Blackletter would have looked like a 1455 contract. In Helvetica it would look like a 1980s passport.",
      "typography": "Typography",
      "typography_inquiry_predict_the_legibil": "🔬 Typography Inquiry — Predict the Legibility",
      "typography_today": "Typography Today",
      "ukiyo_e_pictures_of_the_floating_world": "Ukiyo-e (\"pictures of the floating world\") were full-color woodblock prints made by teams: designer drew the master image, carvers cut a separate block for each color, printer registered each block onto the same paper in sequence. A single complex Hokusai print might use 15-20 blocks. The technical sophistication was unmatched globally until photogravure in the 1880s.",
      "ulysses_james_joyce": "Ulysses (James Joyce)",
      "uncle_tom_s_cabin": "Uncle Tom's Cabin",
      "uncle_tom_s_cabin_1851": "Uncle Tom's Cabin (1851) ",
      "uncle_tom_s_cabin_1852": "Uncle Tom's Cabin (1852)",
      "uncomfortable": "Uncomfortable",
      "underground_comix": "Underground comix",
