      "raptors_fit_the_type_i_pattern_a_steep": "Raptors fit the Type I pattern — a steep cliff in year 1 (70% of juveniles die during their first winter), then a long plateau where most adults survive 5-10+ years. This is why protecting adult breeders is the highest-leverage conservation action. A red-tailed hawk that survives year 1 typically lives to age 6-10; a kestrel that survives year 1 lives to age 5-7. Eagle adults can live 25+ years.",
