      "slide_the_asymmetry_slider_to_100_your": "Slide the asymmetry slider to 100% — your detection radius is tiny + barely larger than a single pixel. Real barn owls can localize sound to ~1° error in pitch dark. Slide to 0% (a hawk's ear placement) — the radius balloons to 40% of the canvas. This is why hawks hunt by sight + owls hunt by sound.",
