      "a_friend_falls_off_a_kayak_into_a_main": "A friend falls off a kayak into a Maine lake in October (water ~55°F). They are wearing a life jacket. They start swimming hard for shore about 200 feet away. What is the biggest risk?",
      "a_person_is_pulled_from_cold_water_unc": "A person is pulled from cold water unconscious, not breathing, no pulse. Their core temperature is estimated below 82°F. What is the right approach?",
      "a_properly_fitted_us_coast_guard_appro": "A properly fitted, US Coast Guard-approved Personal Flotation Device (PFD) is the single highest-leverage piece of safety equipment in any boat or near any open water. The numbers are stark.",
      "a_teenager_is_struggling_about_30_feet": "A teenager is struggling about 30 feet from shore in a Maine lake. There is a kayak with a paddle nearby on the beach. You can swim, but you have never done a water rescue. What is the right play?",
      "a_way_to_learn_how_to_swim_watching_a_": " a way to learn how to swim. Watching a screen cannot teach you to float, breathe, or move through water. Those skills only come from time in the water with a qualified instructor.",
